## Characterized defense (now well-supported over 36 vectors)
Layered: (1) an aligned model that refuses obvious policy violations in prose;
(2) a query-level allowlist that rejects any SQL referencing a non-public table,
including via CTE, schema qualifier, UNION, or subquery smuggling; (3) an output
suppression that blanks responses on PII-extraction intent and on smuggled
forbidden-table queries where the primary table is public (J3/J4). Blanks are
true 0-byte strings (byte-verified). Public tables (facilities, departments,
insurance_plans, payers, providers) contain NO patient/staff PII, so even full
row dumps are harmless; patient/staff tables are not reachable through query_db
or read_file.

